  "report_period": "Week 5 (27th Jan to 3rd Feb 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Post Panamax \"Jupiter N\" 93/2011 Taizhou, China (SS 04/2026, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was committed to Greek buyers W Marine for USD 16,5 mill. Remind you that back in December, the one-year-younger \"TW Manila\" 93/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 04/2027, DD 04/2025) was sold at USD 19 mill. Uglands Rederi have sold their Supramax \"Bonita\" 58/2010 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 09/2025, DD 08/2023, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 15,7 mill. Note that the two-years-older sister vessel \"Navios Amaryllis\" 58/2008 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 05/2027, DD 05/2025) was sold in December at high USD 14 mill. The OHBS Handysize \"Venture Ocean\" 39/2015 Jiangmen, China (SS 10/2025, DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) was committed for low-mid USD 18 mill basis delivery February-March 2023, while the \"TS Bravo\" 39/2015 Shanhaiguan, China (SS 10/2025, DD 08/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 16,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"African Venture\" 34/2012 Chengxi, China (SS 06/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold for mid-high USD 12 mill. Note that the two-years-older \"Mireille Selmer\" 33/2010 Samjin, China (SS 05/2025, DD 08/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at high USD 10 mill. In addition, the sister vessels \"Camila\" & \"Tia Marta\" 34/2015 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 09/2025, DD 01/2024 & SS 09/2025, DD 09/2023, BWTS fitted) were committed to Turkish buyers for USD 19,5 mill each. Remind you that the one-year-older \"Kirishima Sky\" 35/2014 Minaminippon, Japan (SS 05/2025, DD 09/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 16,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Suezmax \"Amoroza\" 159/2001 Hyundai, Korea (SS 12/2025, DD 12/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold to undisclosed buyers for USD 27 mill. For comparison, the two-years-younger \"Kriti Breeze\" 151/2003 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 11/2023) was sold in December at USD 30,5 mill. Indonesian buyers Buana Lintas Lautan have acquired the Aframax \"Marathon\" 105/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) for USD 32 mill. Remind you that a couple of months ago, the one-year-older \"Seatrust\" 114/2004 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) was sold at USD 35 mill. Diamond S Shipping have committed their MR2 \"High Mercury\" 51/2008 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 07/2023) to European buyers for USD 21 mill. Note that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Lila Amazon\" 51/2007 Stx, Korea (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at low USD 20's mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low usd 6,00's fio range. A Capesize was fixed on period at the usd 13,000 pd basis delivery China for 5/8 months employment.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 7,000/9,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 7,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via West Africa were fixed around usd 7,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into Black Sea were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 425K/450K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Philippines nickel ore trips into China were reported at the level of usd 6,000/7,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indonesian sugar trips into South East Asia were fixed around usd 4,000/5,000 pd. Inter- Mediterranean trips via Black Sea were reported at the level of usd 7,000/8,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent with steels were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. South American trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 8,000/9,000 pd. South American trips into China with logs were fixed around usd 14,000 pd. A small Handysize was fixed on period at the usd 9,100 pd basis delivery China for 3/5 months employment."
    }
  },
